// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`ToolRuntime > contributes tool workflow guidance only while tools are visible > tool workflow guidance 1`] = `"When you need or are required to use a tool, emit its structured tool call immediately; describing a call in text does not execute it. Read relevant files and project instructions before changing code, reuse existing patterns, and update affected callers and configuration. Run independent calls together when useful; sequence calls that depend on earlier results or edit the same files. Inspect errors and exit status before choosing the next action. If output is truncated, use the returned path, cursor, or range to retrieve the relevant missing content. A background acknowledgement confirms a start, not completion; use the available status or completion notice to establish the outcome. For action tasks, identify the requested outcome and an observable check before acting. A successful tool result or subagent report alone does not establish completion. Inspect the affected behavior or state with relevant checks, compare the evidence with every requirement, and continue authorized work that remains. If a check fails or is unavailable, report the specific gap and never claim success without evidence. State which requirements are verified and which remain unverified."`;
